+### 2026-11-18 · `spec` · `adr-0043` — Learning from `Awesome-FDE-Roadmap`: four adoptable, three not
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| **Type** | `spec` |
+| **Evidence** | `docs/08-adr/ADR-0043-hoc-tu-fde-roadmap.md` |
+| **Impact** | **No** code change, no new dependency. One ADR plus one entry in `docs/gates/README.md` |
+
+**The first MIT repo in this series.** After four consecutive `license: null` or GPL-3.0 hits
+(`non4me/marble-race`, `non4me/marbles2d`, `livecade/marble-race-*`, `v0-task-manager`), this one is
+readable and learnable. But it is a **curriculum**: 22 files, mostly a 55 KB `README.md`. Learn, do
+not copy.
+
+**A real gap, independent of that repo:** `test-strategy.md` §5 *Measuring quality* lists **9
+metrics** (line coverage, mutation, flaky, fuzz…) and **0** about AI. `ADR-0038` §6 states it itself:
+*"genre classification — ❌ **NOT MEASURED.** No human labels to compare against."* ⇒ The repo runs
+an AI classifier in the request path and has **no measurement** for it.
+
+**Adoptable:** a golden set of **≥ 200 human-labelled games** for `genre_id` plus a **per-class
+confusion matrix** (not a single score), with a precision gate of 0.8 ⇒ below it, **disable** the
+feature and fall back to `source: assumed`. This measures **the classifier against human labels**,
+**not** game quality by AI.
+
+**Forbidden — and this is the easiest place to get it wrong:** the FDE repo recommends
+**Pairwise / Model-as-a-Judge**, which sounds like a natural fit for the existing **Blind Version
+Duel**. But `ADR-0038` §5.2 forbids it: *"version quality is measured by real human play-hours… **Do
+not** put an AI measurement into that chain."* The root reason is `KVU-2` §1.4: the audit unit of an
+AI measurement is `(model, version)` — it measures the **model**, not the **game**.
+
+**Not adopted:** the GCP stack (BigQuery/GKE/VPC SC/ADK/Vertex/LlamaParse — Game9K is Postgres +
+ClickHouse + Solana + Valkey), and `web/` (Vite + React) — the portal is plain `node:http`.
+
+**Checking backwards, and it is uncomfortable:** the FDE repo's **🚩 Red Flags** #1 is *"Data will be
+ready in 2 weeks (It never is)"*. Game9K **shows that signal**: `θ_D7,C` for `idle-incremental` and
+`multiplayer-arena` is `source: assumed`, and `percentile_C` needs **≥ 200 games/genre** while today
+it is **0** — and those three parameters sit on the path of gate `M2`.
+
+Decision: [`ADR-0043`](../docs/08-adr/ADR-0043-hoc-tu-fde-roadmap.md).
+
+### 2026-11-18 · `spec` · `adr-0042` — Do not adopt `v0-task-manager`, do not use Supabase
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| **Type** | `spec` |
+| **Evidence** | `docs/08-adr/ADR-0042-v0-task-manager-va-supabase.md` |
+| **Impact** | **No** code change, no new dependency, **no lines added**. One ADR plus one entry in `docs/gates/README.md` |
+
+**Three independent reasons, each sufficient on its own:**
+
+**① License `null` in both the fork and the upstream.** `gh api ... --jq .license` ⇒ `null`; the
+upstream `dilums/v0-task-manager` is also `null`; **0 LICENSE files**. No license means
+all-rights-reserved. The same boundary `ADR-0016` applied to five other repos.
+
+**② No data layer.** Grepping the full tarball (89 blobs): `supabase` ⇒ **0 files**; `fetch(` /
+`localStorage` / `axios` / `useSWR` ⇒ **0 hits**; `app/api/**` ⇒ **0 files**; task data is a
+**constant in `useState`**. ⇒ There is no database to "move to Supabase" — the two halves of the
+request do not connect.
+
+**③ `portal/` already has the equivalent, and more.** A four-column Kanban board, a drawer with
+`acceptance`, an append-only `issue_events` log, **branch + PR creation from a card**
+(`/api/issues/:key/branch`), quality-gate linking (`gate` + `/handoff`), `policy.mjs` authorisation,
+Postgres persistence, and **514 passing tests**. The other repo has **0 tests**.
+
+**Supabase has been rejected in five places** (ADR-0015 line 142, `docs/10-opensource` lines 39 and
+273, two decision notes). The technical reason: two auth systems ⇒ two `user_id` sources that cannot
+be constrained; Supabase **is** Postgres, so it does not replace Postgres — it inserts a vendor
+**between** the app and the source of truth about money; swapping `policy.mjs` for RLS costs 514 tests.
+
+**Correction inside this ADR:** the first draft claimed *"`issues` has no `estimate`"*. Reading the
+full `CREATE TABLE issues` shows **both `assignee_id` and `points` exist**. That was nearly reporting
+a missing thing that was already there — §5 was fixed rather than left standing.
+
+Decision: [`ADR-0042`](../docs/08-adr/ADR-0042-v0-task-manager-va-supabase.md).
